{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalBlockTrace","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalBlockTrace","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.QJucysMurphyEigen","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeInclusion"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.trace_heckeIncl_mul_lastGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.trace_heckeIncl_mul_lastGen","kind":"theorem","line":270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalBlockTrace.lean#L270-L287","doc":"**The reduction, for a single `V_λ`, stated about an actual Hecke element.**\n\nFor every `y ∈ H_m(q)`, with `σ_{m+1}` the last generator of `H_{m+2}(q)`:\n\n`tr(ρ(ι y) · ρ(σ_{m+1})) = ∑_T ρ(ι y)_{TT} · seminormalParam q (axialDist T (m+1))`.\n\nThis is `χ^λ(x·σ_n) = ∑_T x_{TT} · a(c(λ/μ) − c_T(n))` — the identity the corner reduction of the\nMarkov condition rests on — with the hypothesis now discharged for genuine elements of the\nsubalgebra rather than assumed of a matrix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.seminormalRep_heckeIncl_mem_blockSubalgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.seminormalRep_heckeIncl_mem_blockSubalgebra","kind":"theorem","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalBlockTrace.lean#L246-L268","doc":"**The image of the tower inclusion preserves the blocks.**  For every `y ∈ H_m(q)`, the\nseminormal matrix of `ι y ∈ H_{m+1}(q)` is block-preserving for the top entry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.trace_mul_genMat_of_adjoin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.trace_mul_genMat_of_adjoin","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalBlockTrace.lean#L223-L235","doc":"**The usable form.**  For any `X` in the algebra generated by the generators that avoid `k+1`,\n\n`tr(X · σ_k) = ∑_T X_{TT} · seminormalParam q (axialDist T k)`.\n\nThis is exactly the identity `chi^λ(x · σ_n) = ∑_T x_{TT} a(c(λ/μ) − c_T(n))` that the corner\nreduction of the Markov condition rests on, for a single `V_λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.adjoin_earlyGens_le_blockSubalgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.adjoin_earlyGens_le_blockSubalgebra","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalBlockTrace.lean#L214-L221","doc":"**The whole subalgebra generated by the early generators preserves the blocks**, not merely the\ngenerators themselves.  This is the statement the Markov reduction needs about `H_{N-1} ⊂ H_N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.earlyGens","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.earlyGens","kind":"def","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalBlockTrace.lean#L210-L212","doc":"The generators available to `H_{N-1}`: every `σ_l` that does not touch the entry `N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.genMat_mem_blockSubalgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.genMat_mem_blockSubalgebra","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalBlockTrace.lean#L202-L208","doc":"Every generator `σ_l` with `l + 1 < N` lies in the block subalgebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.blockSubalgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.blockSubalgebra","kind":"def","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalBlockTrace.lean#L188-L200","doc":"The block-preserving matrices form a subalgebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.blockPreserving_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.blockPreserving_mul","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalBlockTrace.lean#L179-L186","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.blockPreserving_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.blockPreserving_neg","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalBlockTrace.lean#L175-L177","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.blockPreserving_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.blockPreserving_smul","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalBlockTrace.lean#L171-L173","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.blockPreserving_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.blockPreserving_add","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalBlockTrace.lean#L167-L169","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.blockPreserving_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.blockPreserving_one","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalBlockTrace.lean#L162-L165","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.blockPreserving_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.blockPreserving_zero","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalBlockTrace.lean#L159-L160","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.BlockPreserving","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.BlockPreserving","kind":"def","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalBlockTrace.lean#L155-L157","doc":"Matrices that respect the decomposition of `SYT μ` by the cell holding the entry `N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.trace_mul_genMat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.trace_mul_genMat","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalBlockTrace.lean#L122-L146","doc":"**The trace identity the Markov reduction runs on.**  For any matrix `X` that preserves the\nblock decomposition by `cellOf · (k+1)` — in particular the image of any element of the subalgebra\ngenerated by `σ_1, …, σ_{k-1}`, by `cellOf_eq_of_genMat_ne_zero` — the trace of `X · σ_k` picks up\nonly the diagonal:\n\n`tr(X · σ_k) = ∑_T X_{TT} · seminormalParam q (axialDist T k)`.\n\nBoth cross terms die: off-diagonal entries of `σ_k` cross blocks, and `X` is zero across blocks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.cellOf_eq_of_genMat_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.cellOf_eq_of_genMat_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalBlockTrace.lean#L106-L120","doc":"An **earlier** generator never moves the cell of `N`: if `σ_l`'s matrix entry between `T'` and\n`T` is nonzero and `l + 1 < N`, then `T'` and `T` agree on the cell of `N`.  This is the statement\nthat `H_{N-1} ⊂ H_N` preserves the block decomposition by `cellOf · N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.genMat_eq_zero_of_cellOf_succ_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.genMat_eq_zero_of_cellOf_succ_eq","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SeminormalBlockTrace.lean#L91-L104","doc":"The seminormal matrix of `σ_k` vanishes off the diagonal between tableaux that agree on the\ncell of `k+1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}